 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Trooper Joseph J. Gallagher Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S5426",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5426-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-o, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5426\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Trooper Joseph J. Gallagher Memorial\nBridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo honor the life and sacrifice of New York State Trooper Joseph J.\nGallagher by naming a part of the Sagtikos Parkway in the Town of Smith-\ntown the \"Trooper Joseph J. Gallagher Memorial Bridge\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the highway law by adding a new section 344-m\n\nSection 2 states the responsibilities of the commissioner of transporta-\ntion\n\nSection 3 effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTrooper Joseph J Gallagher, a seven-year veteran of the New York State\nPolice, was critically injured on December 18, 2017 while on-duty he\nstopped to assist a disabled motorist along an overpass leading to the\nLong Island Expressway. A distracted driver struck Trooper Gallagher as\nhe setup emergency flares in the road to alert oncoming traffic. Sadly,\nTrooper Gallagher succumbed to his injuries on March 26, 2021.\n\nIt is only proper that the bridge where Trooper Gallagher was critically\ninjured be named in his honor.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS6533 2021-2022 Referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
